  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the highest-priority uncertainty is establishing a reliable performance floor. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest possible configuration: a single modality, a single profile (no aggregation complexity), and a deterministic linear encoder (PCA) with no training instability risk. This gives a clean, interpretable baseline accuracy against which all subsequent experiments—alternative RNA encoders, image modality, multiprofile aggregation, and multimodal fusion—can be compared. Choosing the simplest baseline first avoids confounding multiple design choices and ensures that any later improvement is attributable to a specific added component. It is the most uncertainty-reducing use of experiment 1 under a 10-experiment budget."
}

